  "id": "BIT-phpmyadmin-2026-119429",
  "summary": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 Two-Factor Authentication Removal via /config/set",
  "details": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 contains a missing re-authentication vulnerability that allows authenticated attackers to remove two-factor authentication by posting the 2fa key to /config/set. Attackers holding a hijacked session can submit key=2fa with a null JSON value to SetConfigController, stripping 2FA so later logins require only the MySQL password.",
  "aliases": [
    "CVE-2026-119429"
  ],
